# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule, evaluating the MULLER
# (Muller/Buijse-Baerends, Occ_opt/JK_only.h) JK-only RDMFT functional.
# FUNCTIONAL does not need DEBUG -- setting it (as here) makes main.cpp
# generate fractional initial occupations for the converged HF/DHF
# orbitals (Occ_opt/OccupationInit.h; OCCUPATION_INIT PROPORTIONAL by
# default -- an aufbau reference redistributed proportionally into the
# interior box; OCCUPATION_INIT FERMI_DIRAC instead smears at
# TEMPERATURE Kelvin, default 1000), evaluate FUNCTIONAL on them, and
# then OPTIMIZE the occupations at those same fixed orbitals via
# Occ_opt/SQP.h -- all printed right after each "Total ... energy"
# line. With NO FUNCTIONAL keyword at all (see water.inp), this whole
# step is skipped entirely.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER_AS

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
